<title>BAHRAIN: Saudi offers 3.5 bln riyals in latest bonds issue.</title>
<headline>Saudi offers 3.5 bln riyals in latest bonds issue.</headline>
<dateline>MANAMA 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Saudi Arabian Monetary Agency has offered two and three-year government bonds worth 3.5 billion riyals ($933.3 million) to Saudi-based banks, bankers in the kingdom said on Monday.</p>
<p>They said the coupon for two-year bonds worth 2.5 billion riyals and maturing on July 16, 1999 was put at 6.18 percent.</p>
<p>The coupon for three-year bonds worth one billion riyals and maturing on July 16, 2000 was fixed at 6.35 percent. -- Manama newsroom 973-524424 ($ = 3.750 Saudi Arabian Riyals)</p>
</text>
